    "সে",
    "তিনি",
    "ও",
    "উনি",
    "politeness"
   ],
   "rule": null,
   "text": "Bengali has no gender: **সে** is he or she. Instead it marks respect: **আপনি** for strangers and elders, **তুমি** for friends and family, **তুই** for very close friends and children. The verb ending changes with the level, not with gender.",
   "tables": [
    {
     "head": [
      "Meaning",
      "Familiar",
      "Ordinary",
      "Polite"
     ],
     "rows": [
      [
       "you",
       "তুই",
       "তুমি",
       "আপনি"
      ],
      [
       "he / she (far)",
       "—",
       "সে / ও",
       "তিনি / উনি"
      ],
      [
       "I / we",
       "আমি / আমরা",
       "",
       ""
      ],
      [
       "you (plural)",
       "তোরা",
       "তোমরা",
       "আপনারা"
      ],
      [
       "they",
       "—",
       "তারা / ওরা",
       "তাঁরা / ওঁরা"
      ]
     ]
    }
   ],
   "after": null,
   "examples": [
    {
     "text": "আপনি কেমন আছেন?",
     "translation": "How are you? (polite)",
     "note": null,
     "reading": null
    },
    {
     "text": "তুমি কোথায় যাচ্ছ?",
     "translation": "Where are you going? (to a friend)",
     "note": null,
     "reading": null
    },
    {
     "text": "তিনি একজন ডাক্তার।",
     "translation": "He/she is a doctor.",
     "note": "respectful তিনি",
     "reading": null
    }
   ],
   "points": [],
   "tip": null
  },
  {
   "number": 3,
   "id": "classifiers",
   "title": "The, a & plural: -টা, -টি, -গুলো",
   "kind": "structure",
   "level": "A1",
   "tags": [
    "classifier",
    "definite",
    "টা",
    "টি",
    "গুলো",
    "রা",
    "একটা",
    "plural",
    "article"
   ],
   "rule": null,
   "text": "There is no separate word for \"the\": **-টা** (everyday) or **-টি** (a little formal or affectionate) on the noun makes it definite. **একটা** means \"a\". Plurals take **-গুলো** (things) or **-রা** (people); after a number, the noun stays singular: **তিনটা বই** (three books).",
   "tables": [
    {
     "head": [
      "Ending",
      "Meaning",
      "Example"
     ],
     "rows": [
      [
       "{টা} / {টি}",
       "the (one)",
       "বইটা | the book"
      ],
      [
       "একটা / একটি",
       "a, one",
       "একটা বই | a book"
      ],
      [
       "{গুলো} / {গুলি}",
       "the (several things)",
       "বইগুলো | the books"
      ],
      [
       "{রা} / {এরা}",
       "plural of people",
       "ছাত্ররা | the students"
      ]
     ]
    }
   ],
   "after": null,
   "examples": [
    {
     "text": "ছেলেটা খুব ভালো।",
     "translation": "The boy is very nice.",
     "note": null,
     "reading": null
    },
    {
     "text": "আমি একটা নতুন জামা কিনেছি।",
     "translation": "I bought a new shirt.",
     "note": null,
     "reading": null
    },
    {
     "text": "আমগুলো খুব মিষ্টি।",
     "translation": "The mangoes are very sweet.",
     "note": "-গুলো for things",
     "reading": null
    }
   ],
   "points": [],
   "tip": null
  },
  {
   "number": 4,
   "id": "cases",
   "title": "Case endings: -কে, -র, -তে",
   "kind": "structure",
   "level": "A2",
   "tags": [
    "case",
    "কে",
    "র",
    "এর",
    "তে",
    "এ",
    "object",
    "possessive",
    "location",
    "genitive",
    "locative"
   ],
   "rule": null,
   "text": "Endings attach to the noun (after any -টা/-গুলো): **ছেলেটাকে** (the boy, as object), **বইটার** (of the book), **ঘরে** (in the room). After a vowel, use **-র** and **-তে/-য়**; after a consonant, **-এর** and **-এ**. Possessive pronouns: **আমার, তোমার, আপনার, তার, আমাদের**.",
   "tables": [
    {
     "head": [
      "Ending",
      "Use",
      "Example"
     ],
     "rows": [
      [
       "{কে} / {এরকে}",
       "object (people), to",
       "রহিমকে বলো | tell Rahim"
      ],
      [
       "{র} / {এর}",
       "of, 's",
       "রহিমের বাড়ি | Rahim's house"
      ],
      [
       "{তে} / {এ}",
       "in, at, on",
       "বাড়িতে ;; ঢাকায় | at home ;; in Dhaka"
      ]
     ]
    }
   ],
   "after": null,
   "examples": [
    {
     "text": "আমি মাকে ফোন করেছি।",
     "translation": "I called Mum.",
     "note": "মা + কে",
     "reading": null
    },
    {
     "text": "এটা আমার বোনের ঘর।",
     "translation": "This is my sister's room.",
     "note": "বোন + এর",
     "reading": null
    },
    {
     "text": "ওরা কলকাতায় থাকে।",
     "translation": "They live in Kolkata.",
     "note": "কলকাতা + য়",
     "reading": null
    }
   ],
   "points": [],
   "tip": null
  },
  {
   "number": 5,
   "id": "postpositions",
   "title": "Postpositions (জন্য, সঙ্গে, থেকে…)",
